---
system: sys-13-security-secrets-management
flow_id: brute-force-detection-and-block
surface: internal-RPC
spec_anchor: /software/systems/13-security-secrets-management#security-event-detection-rules
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, IdentityService, BruteForceDetector, Redis, PostgreSQL, PagerDuty]
apis:
  - POST /v1/auth/login
externals: [PagerDuty]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - ip_already_blocked
  - escalation_24h_block
  - postgres_insert_failed
  - pagerduty_publish_failed
idempotency: SET NX on ip_block:{ip} with EX prevents double-block; ip_block_list row keyed by id with append-only updates
retry: PagerDuty escalation publish retried with backoff
timeout: 50ms p99 per detector call
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant IdentityService
    participant BruteForceDetector
    participant Redis
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant PagerDuty

    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/auth/login {email, password}
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward (after sys-17 rate limit)
    IdentityService->>BruteForceDetector: checkLoginAttempt(ip, success=false, userId?)
    BruteForceDetector->>Redis: GET ip_block:{ip}
    alt ip_already_blocked
        Redis-->>BruteForceDetector: "1"
        BruteForceDetector-->>IdentityService: {blocked: true}
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 429 login_rate_limited
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 429
    else not_blocked
        Redis-->>BruteForceDetector: nil
        BruteForceDetector->>Redis: ZADD login_attempts:{ip} {now}:{success_flag}
        BruteForceDetector->>Redis: EXPIRE login_attempts:{ip} 600
        BruteForceDetector->>Redis: ZREMRANGEBYSCORE login_attempts:{ip} 0 (now - 5min)
        BruteForceDetector->>Redis: ZRANGEBYSCORE login_attempts:{ip} (now - 5min) now
        Redis-->>BruteForceDetector: attempts[]

        alt failure_threshold_exceeded (>=10 failures in 5min)
            BruteForceDetector->>Redis: GET ip_block_count:{ip}
            Redis-->>BruteForceDetector: prev_block_count
            alt escalation_24h_block (block_count >= 2 → 3rd block in 24h)
                BruteForceDetector->>Redis: SET ip_block:{ip} 1 EX 86400 (24h)
            else first_or_second_block
                BruteForceDetector->>Redis: SET ip_block:{ip} 1 EX 3600 (1h)
            end
            BruteForceDetector->>Redis: INCR ip_block_count:{ip}
            BruteForceDetector->>PostgreSQL: INSERT security_events {event_type='brute_force_detected', severity='warning'|'critical'}
            BruteForceDetector->>PostgreSQL: INSERT ip_block_list {ip_address, reason, expires_at, security_event_id}
            alt postgres_insert_failed
                PostgreSQL--xBruteForceDetector: error
                Note over BruteForceDetector: log and retry async — Redis block remains active (security-first)
            end
            alt escalated_to_critical
                BruteForceDetector->>PagerDuty: page security team {ip, block_count, severity='critical'}
                alt pagerduty_publish_failed
                    PagerDuty--xBruteForceDetector: 5xx
                    Note over BruteForceDetector: retry with backoff
                end
            end
            BruteForceDetector-->>IdentityService: {blocked: true}
        else under_threshold
            BruteForceDetector-->>IdentityService: {blocked: false}
        end
    end

    Note over BruteForceDetector,PagerDuty: 10 fails / 5min → 1h block · 3 blocks / 24h → 24h block · security-first (Redis block holds even if PostgreSQL audit insert fails)
